\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Shared representation and learning stages of SCIT-Speech. \textbf  {a}, The fixed $L=3$ interface maps speech to 50-Hz latent frames and transmits three 10-bit indices per frame. Local codebook lookup and summation provide the representation for waveform decoding. \textbf  {b}, Teacher-aligned architecture search precedes joint codec training to obtain SCIT. Channel-aware fine-tuning produces SCIT-LCA, which is subsequently frozen for the identification study. The communication objective combines perturbed-speech reconstruction and clean--perturbed consistency. \textbf  {c}, Receiver-side identification reads both the received indices and their reconstructed waveform. The token encoder, audio projection, fusion gate and classifier are trainable; the speech codec and ECAPA-TDNN backbone are frozen. Both branches produce 256-dimensional embeddings. No additional speaker embedding is transmitted.}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rv3-components}{{1}{2}{}{figure.1}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {2.3}The 1.5-kbit/s codec improves objective reconstruction scores}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sec:rv3-quality}{{2.3}{2}{}{subsection.2.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Resource-efficient encoder selection at a fixed latent interface. \textbf  {a}, Encoder parameter counts and MACs for 8,192 profiled configuration candidates. The triangle identifies the hand-designed reference and the star identifies the subsequently selected architecture. Both axes are logarithmic; each point represents a configuration profile. \textbf  {b}, Selected-encoder resource requirements normalized to the reference. RTF was measured for encoder FP32 inference on an RTX 5070 Ti using a one-second input and averaging five synchronized passes.}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rv3-nas}{{2}{3}{}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Clean-channel reconstruction on 300 LibriSpeech test-clean utterances. Entries are means [95\% utterance-bootstrap intervals]. The first three codecs share the nominal 1.5-kbit/s operating point; bold means identify the best in that group. Opus and PCM are higher-rate references. Lower mel-L1 and higher STOI/PESQ-WB are better.}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:rv3-quality}{{1}{3}{}{table.1}{}}
